# AXIS CELL: pattern kind = `PWildcard` written as `case _:` (as opposed to the
# `else:` spelling, which the parser desugars to the same node). The two
# spellings are the same node to the self-host and DIFFERENT to Rust, which is
# what this cell exists to pin.
#
# ⚠ DELIBERATE, RATIFIED SH<->Rust DIVERGENCE -- never "corrected" toward Rust.
# `gg check` REJECTS this program (rc 1, `E_UseAfterMove`) because its
# fall-through suppression keys on a syntactic `else_arm` alone and does not
# credit an unguarded `case _:`. The arm IS a catch-all, so Rust is
# over-rejecting a provably-safe program and the self-host is strictly more
# precise. See the `TODO.md` entry beginning "production OVER-REJECTION (false
# positive), from RV-D pass-1" (grep `check_stmt.rs:1217-1222` in `TODO.md`).
#
# This is also the only cell in the net that catches a "faithful-to-Rust"
# reimplementation of the divergence gate that keys on the desugared `else:`
# arm's degenerate `Span(start, start)` sentinel instead of on the pattern:
# `match_else_arm_diverge_accept.gg` passes such an implementation, this does not.
#
# RED-VERIFY (make the gate unconditional): same break as
# `match_else_arm_diverge_accept.gg` -- replace the `SMatch` arm of
# `live_stmt_diverges` with a bare `return false`. Measured: this cell flips
# rc 0 -> rc 1 (E_UseAfterMove, 0 bytes of C).
void sink(String ^x):
    pass

void probe(int n, bool c):
    String s = "hello"
    if c:
        sink(^s)
        match n:
            case 1:
                return
            case 2:
                return
            case _:
                return
    print(s)

void main():
    probe(3, true)
